<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in Friday's</p>
<p>men's 4x10-km cross-country relay at the Nordic skiing world</p>
<p>championships:</p>
<p>1. Norway (Sture Sivertsen, Erling Jevne, Bjorn Daehlie, Thomas</p>
<p>Alsgaard) One hour 37 minutes 06.10 seconds</p>
<p>2. Finland (Harri Kirvesniemi, Mika Myllylae, Jari Raesaenen,</p>
<p>Jaro Isometsae) 1:39:17.30</p>
<p>3. Italy (Giorgio di Centa, Silvio Fauner, Pietro Piller</p>
<p>Cottrer, Fulvio Valbusa) 1:39:56.90</p>
<p>4. Russia (Sergei Chepikov, Sergei Chernykh, Maksim Pitschugin,</p>
<p>Alexei Prokurorov) 1:39:57.10</p>
<p>5. Sweden (Mathias Fredriksson, Anders Bergstroem, Torgny</p>
<p>Mogren, Henrik Forsberg) 1:40:43.10</p>
<p>6. Germany (Uwe Bellmann, Jochen Behle, Rene Sommerfeldt,</p>
<p>Johann Muehlegg) 1:40:43.20</p>
<p>7. Belarus (Sergei Dolidowitch, Alexei Tregoubov, Alexander</p>
<p>Sannikov, Viatcheslav Plaksunov) 1:41:25.20</p>
<p>8. Czech Republic (Lubomir Buchta, Lukas Bauer, Petr Michl,</p>
<p>Vaclav Korunka) 1:41:56.00</p>
<p>9. Slovakia (Ivan Batory, Martin Bakcicak, Andrej Paricka,</p>
<p>Stanislav Jezik) 1:42:25.10</p>
<p>10. Canada (Donald Farley, Robin McKeever, Chris Blanchard,</p>
<p>Guido Visser) 1:42:29.80</p>
<p>11. Estonia (Andrus Veerpalu, Raul Olle, Elmo Kassin, Jaak Mae)</p>
<p>1:43:04.70</p>
<p>12. Kazakhstan (Andrei Nevzorov, Pavel Ryabinin, Konstantin</p>
<p>Bratoshov, Vitalii Lilicenko) 1:44:46.20</p>
<p>13. Austria (Markus Glander, Alois Stadlober, Christian</p>
<p>Hoffmann, Achim Walcher) 1:44:58.20</p>
<p>14. Japan (Katsuhito Ebisawa, Hiroyuki Imai, Mitsuo Horigome,</p>
<p>Masaaki Kouzu) 1:44:58.90</p>
<p>15. Unites States (Marcus Nash, Patrick Weaver, Carl Swenson,</p>
<p>Justin Wadsworth) 1:46:20.50</p>
<p>16. Ukraine (Pavel Zabolotnyi, Alexander Ushalenko, Mikhail</p>
<p>Artioukhov, Nikolai Popovich) 1:46:48.70</p>
<p>17. Poland (Janusz Krezelok, Ryszard Labay, Krzystof Wanczyk,</p>
<p>Marcin Rozkowski) 1:47:05.50</p>
</text>
